{"fingerprint":"ceaae520582628afd98bbbe179f69bab9913d584aa1c216e8b6f0230a06d96c9","path":"src/review_gauntlet/review_adapter.py","rule_id":"data-validation","content":"`_read_cell_file_metadata` reads the file from the current working tree regardless of `review_commit`. The returned `line_count` is then used in `_validated_comments_for_cell` (line 635) to hard-fail any comment whose `end_line` exceeds it. When `review_commit` points to an older commit where the file was longer, valid line references are incorrectly rejected; when the file has since grown, out-of-range references incorrectly pass. The metadata should be derived from the commit being reviewed.","suggestion_code":"    def _read_cell_file_metadata(self, cell: ReviewCell) -> FileMetadata:
